WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:05.000
Welcome to the Eager to be Healthy Podcast. I am Dr. Michael, your host.

00:05.000 --> 00:10.500
Today, we are discussing the foundational pillars of health and longevity.

00:10.500 --> 00:15.800
Many people ask me, "Dr. Michael, what is the single most important habit for my health?"

00:15.800 --> 00:22.000
The truth is, it isn't a magic pill. It is the combination of sleep, movement, and nutrition.

00:22.000 --> 00:27.500
Let us start with sleep. Sleep is the ultimate biological restorative mechanism.

00:27.500 --> 00:34.200
Without seven to eight hours of high-quality sleep, your cognitive performance and immune system suffer.

00:34.200 --> 00:40.000
In fact, chronic sleep deprivation is linked to heart disease, diabetes, and memory decline.

00:40.000 --> 00:46.500
So, make sleep a non-negotiable priority in your daily schedule. Create a sleep sanctuary.

00:46.500 --> 00:52.000
Next is movement. Your body was designed to move, not sit at a desk all day.

00:52.000 --> 00:58.500
Regular physical activity—even just a thirty-minute brisk walk—boosts your mood and keeps blood vessels healthy.

00:58.500 --> 01:05.000
Try to incorporate strength training at least twice a week. Muscle mass is a strong predictor of longevity.

01:05.000 --> 01:11.200
Finally, let us talk about nutrition. Focus on eating whole foods—vegetables, fruits, and clean proteins.

01:11.200 --> 01:17.500
Minimize processed sugars and refined carbohydrates. They trigger inflammation and lead to energy crashes.

01:17.500 --> 01:23.000
Drink plenty of water throughout the day, and limit caffeine consumption to the morning.

01:23.000 --> 01:28.000
If you implement these three pillars, you will notice a dramatic improvement in your vitality.

01:28.000 --> 01:34.500
Thank you for listening to this episode. Remember to check out your settings to customize your DoggCatcher queue!

01:34.500 --> 01:40.000
In our next episode, we will detail how to design your sleep sanctuary. Until then, stay eager to be healthy!
